description.narrative:
War Child UK suspended its activities in the Bamingui-Bangoran prefecture for a period of 12 months due to the prevailing insecurity in the region which negatively impacted the organisation's office. This projects aim to replicate and consolidate the efforts put in place by War Child UK in 2020, notably through:

Support to the reintegration of CAAFAG and other children at risk through a community-based resource case management approach with community case managers (follow-up of 250 reintegrated in 2019-20, and reintegration of 180 new children);

Holistic support to 50 GBV survivors and 40 Unaccompanied/Separated Children through a community resource-based case management approach with community case managers;

Community-based psychosocial support to children through safe child-friendly spaces already established and facilitated by youth clubs (peer educators) supported to conduct sports and recreational activities with their peers with the support of community case managers and RECOPE;

Strengthening of the protective environment for children through RECOPE and birth registration.
